            <div xml:id="d1271">

                <pb facs="1015" n="899" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg899"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.2311/71.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Governor of Texas to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Austin, Texas</hi></placeName>.<lb/>[<date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-09-30">undated</date>] (Received October
                        1, 1912—1.15 p.m.)</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your telegram this date answering mine of yesterday in which I withdraw consent
                    for passing Mexican troops over Texas territory received. If Mexican Government
                    will amend request so as to eliminate Marathon and detrain Mexican troops at Del
                    Rio, I will have no objection to urge, but after reflection I could not give
                    consent to detraining Mexican troops at Marathon and marching them over rough,
                    dry country 75 miles and invite a conflict from Orozco’s men, who, according to
                    my advices, are now operating across the Rio Grande River in Mexico from the
                    Marathon section of Texas. It would be like inviting a slaughter of unarmed
                    foreign troops on Texas soil. I am pleased to note your suspension of permission
                    for Mexican troops to pass through Texas on receipt of my objections. The
                    objection will be withdrawn if the application is amended as suggested.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">O. B. Colquitt.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
